[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have been writing a metaprogram that works with the <code>.fixpoint_induct</code> theorem generated for partial fixpoints, but it seems that this is not actually added to the environment until syntax with the full name of the theorem is elaborated. I found a workaround by passing the syntax through the elaborator, but I'm not sure if this is intended behavior.</p>\n<p>For example, in this file, env.contains will return <code>true</code>, but if you comment out the reference to <code>simple_diverge.fixpoint_induct</code>, then it will return <code>false</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simple_diverge</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simple_diverge</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"test_fi_exists\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getEnv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"contains? {env.contains (``simple_diverge ++ `fixpoint_induct)}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">use_it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simple_diverge</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">test_fi_exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this prints true, but if you comment `use_it` then it prints false</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602621282,
        "sender_full_name": "Jacob Prinz",
        "timestamp": 1781290550
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You are searching for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.executeReservedNameAction#doc\">docs#Lean.executeReservedNameAction</a>. To explain it simply, we don't want to eagerly generate these lemmas because they would be mostly unused so they get reserved name handlers (you can even register them yourself in an <code>initialize</code> block through <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.registerReservedNameAction#doc\">docs#Lean.registerReservedNameAction</a>). These are run every time an identifier syntax is resolved using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.realizeGlobalConstNoOverload#doc\">docs#Lean.realizeGlobalConstNoOverload</a> (which happens for most identifiers) so as a user you don't notice that the constants don't exist at first. Anyways, here's a modification of your code that works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simple_diverge</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simple_diverge</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: contains? false</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: contains? true</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"contains? {(← getEnv).contains (`simple_diverge.fixpoint_induct)}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">executeReservedNameAction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`simple_diverge.fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"contains? {(← getEnv).contains (`simple_diverge.fixpoint_induct)}\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602651070,
